			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Extend extensions poll timeout and add gRPC shutdown guard\n\nIncrease the polling timeout in `extensions:getInstalled` from 3s to 5s because cold-cache runs over 113 extensions across 6 paths regularly hit ~2950ms, poisoning the workbench's `IExtensionService` cache with empty results.\n\nAdd a process-wide shutdown flag to the Vine gRPC client that gets marked before SIGKILL of Cocoon. Background tasks (PTY reader, file watchers, diagnostics emitter) that fire `SendNotification` after the sidecar is dead now short-circuit silently instead of logging false-positive `Connection refused` errors during shutdown. `SendRequest` returns an error immediately while `SendNotification` returns `Ok(())` to allow natural unwinding of background tasks.\n\nThis prevents the shutdown tail from being flooded with spurious gRPC errors while keeping the worst-case visible boot delay bounded at 5 seconds.",
			"SHA": "06be111688dffce33846936c513b1b67504248a5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T22:18:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				11
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Centralize sky event emissions via LogSkyEmit and add defensive guards\n\nThis commit consolidates all Tauri event emissions through `LogSkyEmit` for histogram visibility in the `[DEV:SKY-EMIT]` tracking channel, and adds defensive error handling throughout the provider layer.\n\n**LogSkyEmit migration (7 files):**\n- LifecyclePhaseState, WorkspaceDelta, DiagnosticProvider, OpenDocument, TerminalProvider, RegisterCommand, RegisterScmProvider\n- Previously each file imported `tauri::Emitter` directly; now routes through LogSkyEmit so diagnostic/command/workspace event volume is visible in the histogram for debugging \"panel shows count but no items\" issues.\n\n**Defensive URI handling (DiagnosticProvider):**\n- Batch now tolerates malformed URIs per entry rather than failing the entire batch (mirrors VS Code's `MarkerService._toMarker` returning undefined instead of throwing)\n- Skips entries with empty URI strings with a warning log\n\n**Defensive path guards:**\n- PathSecurity.rs: Reject empty paths upfront to prevent empty-string path from bypassing workspace gating (`Path::starts_with(\"\")` returns true)\n- FileSystem.rs (CreateEffect): Add empty-path guards for ReadFile and StatFile, returning FileNotFound per VS Code's FileSystemProvider contract\n\n**Terminal resilience (WindServiceHandlers):**\n- localPty:createProcess now returns explicit error when id is 0/invalid instead of silently returning 0 (prevents keystrokes being swallowed)\n- localPty:resize clamps cols/rows to minimum of 1 (portable-pty crashes on 0×0 during pane drag-storms)\n- Resize on disposed terminal now logs warn and returns Null instead of error (common race during shutdown)\n- Tree-view data shape check: force `{items: []}` for non-conforming shapes to prevent TypeError in renderer\n\n**Documentation:**\n- MarkerDataDTO: Clarify coordinates are 1-based (matching workbench IMarkerData), noting Cocoon's LanguagesNamespace.ts adds the +1 offset from vscode.Position 0-based convention",
			"SHA": "51f75f11010ab398a1f34525834f36b792dfbbfd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:51:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Fix boot-time extensions race and add missing getLatency\n\nAdd polling to extensions:getInstalled to resolve boot-time race condition where workbench caches empty extension list before ExtensionPopulate completes its scan (~250-500ms). Poll the ScannedExtensions map for up to 3 seconds before returning empty, ensuring 113+ extension contributions appear in the activity bar.\n\nAlso add localPty:getLatency handler returning empty array per VS Code's IPtyHostLatencyMeasurement[] contract. Without this, every poll cycle logged \"Unknown IPC command: localPty:getLatency\" and a failed TauriInvoke.",
			"SHA": "2b89f60a78bc0322f8e68c9ae88d722fd369416f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:38:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Remove duplicate DevTools window in debug builds\n\nWindowBuild.rs was calling `MainWindow.open_devtools()` independently\nfrom AppLifecycle.rs, causing two DevTools windows to open on every\ndebug launch. Remove the redundant call and document that DevTools\nauto-open lives in AppLifecycle (line 174), gated on debug_assertions\nwith a matching log line.\n\ndocs(Mountain): Clarify diagnostic coordinates are 1-based\n\nUpdate DiagnosticProvider.rs docstring to specify that\nStartLineNumber/StartColumn and EndLineNumber/EndColumn use 1-based\nindexing, matching workbench IMarkerData. Add note explaining that\nCocoon's LanguagesNamespace.ts NormaliseDiagnostic adds the +1 offset\nfrom vscode.Position 0-based convention before sending to Mountain.",
			"SHA": "c661d669a5f51174397956c2ab363d240e270059"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:42:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Defer sky://terminal/create event to fix race condition\n\nThe terminal workbench's `LocalTerminalBackend.createProcess` flow has a timing vulnerability: when `sky://terminal/create` emits synchronously during step 1 (RPC in-flight), the Tauri event arrives before step 3 (`_ptys.set(id, pty)`) completes. This causes `_ptys.get(id)` to return `undefined`, skipping `handleReady` and preventing `processManager._onProcessReady` from firing. Since `ptyProcessReady` never resolves, every subsequent `processManager.write(data)` call hangs indefinitely—users see the terminal panel but all keystrokes are silently dropped.\n\nFix by emitting on a deferred tokio task with a 120ms delay, giving the RPC response roundtrip + `_ptys.set` sufficient headroom. Also switch to `LogSkyEmit` for visibility under `[DEV:SKY-EMIT]` histogram tracking.\n\nThis complements the existing `AppendTerminalOutput` replay buffer for data (added in c99ccbe), completing the terminal race-condition fix for both create and data events.",
			"SHA": "c2d0beca968f600d76ac4d85a436931124cfdf07"
		}
	],
